  "reason": "The set strongly supports reconstruction of the broad result. R8 reports SPS at exactly 1000 °C on milled CoCrFeNiTi powder, a compositionally close transition-metal HEA, producing a dense, fine-grained material with nanoprecipitates. R1 likewise applies SPS to an Al-Co-Fe-Ni-Ti-containing HEA and observes an additional precipitated phase without coarsening. R2, R6, R10, and R18 establish that mechanically alloyed BCC HEAs subjected to SPS commonly develop oxide or other secondary-phase dispersions, while R5 and R12 reinforce the ball-milling/SPS route. Independently, R9, R13, and R19 show that Al-, Cr-, or Ti-containing HEAs/RHEAs gain oxidation or corrosion resistance through protective oxide scales, and R17 connects heterogeneous HEA microstructure to local electrochemical behavior in chloride media. Together these records would plausibly lead an expert to test 1000 °C SPS of the stated BCC powder and attribute improved density, hardness, oxidation resistance, and chloride corrosion resistance to oxide precipitation and protective-film formation. The exact MgAlTiVFeCo composition, specific spinel/ilmenite oxides, polarization behavior, and biphasic parabolic oxidation kinetics a"
